. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Hypothesis: Having a higher proportion of daughters increases suppo
> rt for gender equality
.         * Model: 2SLS IV regression with gendereq as DV, prop_daughters as en
> dogenous IV, and first_child_female as instrument
.         * Controls: sex, partner, germborn, westgerm, pgbilzeit, age_sq, ln_h
> ghinc, and number of children dummies
. 
.         ivregress 2sls gendereq (prop_daughters = first_child_female) ///
>                 sex partner germborn westgerm pgbilzeit age age_sq ln_hghinc 
> kids_*, vce(robust)
note: kids_0 omitted because of collinearity.
note: kids_8plus omitted because of collinearity.

